1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,582
You see water on the road ahead

2
00:00:01,582 --> 00:00:02,794
but it's never really there

3
00:00:02,794 --> 00:00:03,273
Why?

4
00:00:03,473 --> 00:00:04,665
The sun bakes the asphalt

5
00:00:04,665 --> 00:00:06,231
and the asphalt heats the air above it

6
00:00:06,231 --> 00:00:07,944
so the air near the ground is hottest

7
00:00:08,144 --> 00:00:10,347
Light changes speed between hot and cool air

8
00:00:10,347 --> 00:00:11,990
so it bends instead of going straight

9
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:14,014
Sky light dips down… then curves up

10
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:15,145
into your eye from below

11
00:00:15,345 --> 00:00:17,031
Your brain assumes light travels straight

12
00:00:17,031 --> 00:00:18,569
so it sees the sky on the ground

13
00:00:18,569 --> 00:00:19,717
and it looks like a puddle

14
00:00:19,917 --> 00:00:21,626
Drive closer, and it moves away

15
00:00:21,626 --> 00:00:23,098
because the angle keeps changing

16
00:00:23,298 --> 00:00:24,548
So what you saw wasn't water

17
00:00:24,548 --> 00:00:25,905
it was a picture of the sky!
